  "body": "At [Step 10](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dnd.html#drag-and-drop-processing-model:event-pointercancel) in Drag and Drop processing model, the `pointercancel` could be sent to the Text node (as per [Step 3](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dnd.html#source-node)).  Is this expected?\r\n\r\nIn particular, a `pointerdown` is _not_ sent to a Text node either in Chrome or in Firefox.  But if a text selection is dragged, a `pointercancel` is sent to:\r\n- the parent Element in Chrome (matching the `pointerdown` behavior I just mentioned), and\r\n- the Text node in Firefox (matching the DnD spec).\r\n\r\nThis has been reported in [this Chrome bug](https://crbug.com/1374282).\r\n\r\nWithout a hit-testing algorithm in spec, it is hard for me to say which of these two behaviors is desired!\r\n\r\nAny thoughts? @smaug---- ",
